        "text": "Bash {\"command\": \"cd /d/Dev/AI/agents; S=\\\"C:/Users/fimar/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/D--Dev-AI-agents/e8a614d1-326c-401c-b9bd-a1840afd2559/scratchpad\\\"; cat > \\\"$S/strike56.md\\\" <<'EOF'\\n\\n**Struck 2026-10-25 — a shared index, no add at all.** A session landing S9's new sentence staged\\nits four files by name, the register's own hunk as a blob, and ran the checks before committing.\\nIn those seconds a session planning 01-0011.0110.0090 ran its commit, 588d90e, without naming\\npaths: the index held both sessions' staging, and the S9 rule, its reinstall in the entry file,\\nv129 and this register's line went out under that session's subject and were pushed. Nothing was\\nlost; the history names the wrong step. The same class as the entry's: a staging command that\\ncannot obey *commit the work in current session only*, here `git commit` with no paths, which\\ntakes whatever the shared index holds. Staging by name, the amendment above, would not have\\nstopped it.\\n\\n**Proposed amendment**, to `/commit`, replacing the sentence above, at the self-improvement dial —\\na rule, shown before it lands; a host hook refusing a bare `git commit` in a tree where other\\nsessions run would hold it mechanically:\\n\\n> Commit with the paths named, `git commit -- <file>…`, each one this session wrote or moved, and\\n> stage nothing ahead of the commit; never a directory, a glob, `-A` or a bare `git commit` — in a\\n> tree where other sessions run, the index is shared.\\n\\n**Disposition:** open, struck once.\\nEOF\\nuv run --offline --no-project python - \\\"$S\\\" <<'PYEOF'\\nimport sys, pathlib, subprocess\\nS = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]); add = (S/'strike56.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')\\na = \\\"the proposed sentence stands here as a candidate for a repeat.\\\\n\\\"\\ndef ins(t):\\n    assert t.count(a) == 1; return t.replace(a, a + add)\\nw = pathlib.Path('docs/rule-failures.md'); w.write_text(ins(w.read_text(encoding='utf-8')), encoding='utf-8', newline='')\\nhead = subprocess.run(['git','show','HEAD:docs/rule-failures.md'], capture_output=True).stdout.decode('utf-8')\\n(S/'rf_staged3.md').write_text(ins(head), encoding='utf-8', newline='')\\nPYEOF\\ngit diff --cached --quiet && h=$(git hash-object -w \\\"$S/rf_staged3.md\\\") && git update-index --cacheinfo 100644,$h,docs/rule-failures.md && git diff --cached --numstat && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\\nREGISTER: rule failure 56 struck — another session's bare commit, 588d90e, took this session's staged S9 rule, its reinstall, v129 and the register's line; the amendment to /commit proposed, commit with the paths named; the user, 2026-10-25\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEOF\\ngit log --oneline -1; git push -q 2>&1 | tail -2; git status -sb | head -1; git diff --numstat docs/rule-failures.md\", \"description\": \"Strike 56 and commit only that hunk\"}"
